T3 Code on OpenRC

This package installs an OpenRC adapter, not T3 Code. Installing it does not
download, initialize, enable, start or restart anything. Portage owns
/etc/init.d/t3code, /etc/conf.d/t3code and /usr/libexec/t3code-openrc;
upstream owns the T3 runtime and the service account owns its state and logs.

Replacing an existing service: a custom /usr/local/libexec/t3code-service or
other wrapper is left alone. Back up the service state and database, stop the
old service yourself, never run two supervisors against one T3 home, and
merge config-protect updates (dispatch-conf) deliberately. Protocol-2 Node
runtimes and copied launchers are incompatible and need a separate, backed-up
migration; "initialize" refuses any existing state.

1. As the non-root service user, install the runtime. Read the script first,
   and never run "t3 service install" on OpenRC (upstream's service manager
   integration expects systemd):

     curl --fail --location --output ./t3-install.sh https://t3.codes/install.sh
     less ./t3-install.sh
     t3_home="$HOME/.t3"
     T3CODE_CHANNEL=nightly T3CODE_HOME="$t3_home" sh ./t3-install.sh
     "$HOME/.local/bin/t3" --version

2. Initialize it with the exact installed SemVer in upstream's spelling: keep
   any -nightly and build suffix, no leading "v", not the Gentoo _pre
   spelling and not "nightly". Use the same t3_home as above:

     T3CODE_HOME="$t3_home" /usr/libexec/t3code-openrc initialize VERSION
     T3CODE_HOME="$t3_home" /usr/libexec/t3code-openrc check

3. As administrator set t3code_user and t3code_home (the same absolute
   t3_home path) in /etc/conf.d/t3code and merge any config-protect update.
   Codex, Claude or OpenCode helpers must be installed for that account.
   Then enable and start the service yourself:

     rc-update add t3code default
     rc-service t3code start

4. Verify with the environment descriptor, not a guessed /health path. It
   must show the installed version and capabilities.serverSelfUpdate ==
   "boot-service" (set port to your t3code_port, default 3773):

     port=3773
     curl --fail --silent --noproxy '*' http://127.0.0.1:$port/.well-known/t3/environment | jq .

Troubleshooting: a missing or incomplete runtime is a startup failure, never
bootstrapped. The service log is userdata/logs/openrc.log under t3code_home.
Optional Tailscale Serve (USE=tailscale) is documented next to its options in
/etc/conf.d/t3code.
